  "title": "Transforming Residual Wastewater into Biogas",
  "summary": "Within the Acordionero Forestry Centre, Gran Tierra Energy installed residential-scale anaerobic biodigesters. Biodigesters are systems that break down organic materials, such as food waste, agricultural residues, animal manure and wastewater, through a biological process called anaerobic digestion. In many rural Colombian villages, untreated wastewater flows through open sewers, creating serious health and environmental risks—especially during […]",
